Package: samba
Architecture: linux-any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: pure-Go SMB2/SMB3 file server (zero-copy reads, multichannel)
 A from-scratch SMB2/SMB3 file server written entirely in Go: no CGO, no
 unsafe. It speaks SMB 2.0.2 through 3.1.1 with NTLMv2
 authentication, SMB2/3 signing, SMB 3.1.1 preauth integrity, SMB3
 multichannel, and SMB3 encryption (AES-128/256-GCM and -CCM), plus
 byte-range locks, leases, and directory change notification.
 .
 Large unsigned reads move file pages to the socket through splice(2) without
 ever entering userspace, and the host facilities the server needs (a shared
 listening port, directory watching, byte-range locks, file-to-socket copies)
 are native on Linux.
 .
 Requires the capability to bind port 445. The package is Linux-only because
 this is the Linux distribution's package: the same source builds and runs on
 macOS, the BSDs and Windows, where those facilities use the platform's own
 mechanism or a documented fallback (see the README support table).
